The Engagement Lead is managing the Delivery Team, progress and scope for the outcome in delivery, financial progress, recovery from deviations, and a strong customer relationship. When they are doing a good job, they are running the day-to-day of the engagement, while also strategically considering how they can ensure the team is supported for success, client expectations are tightly managed, and the team is able to deliver Customer Love. They have overall accountability for a successful outcome, no matter the blockers. Some tasks they may have throughout an engagement include:
	• Drafting the Slalom kick-off deck
	• Leading the team through brainstorming ideas for the Customer Love Plan
	• Establishing and maintaining The Big 3 for Delivery Success for the engagement
	• Working with the DE team to address overburn due to heroics
	• Completing Engagement Pulse every week
	• Hosting weekly meetings with the DE team to discuss engagements, progress, issues, and risk
	• Managing client expectations and commitments with last-minute out-of-scope requests
	• Completing a Customer Story to ensure others know the great outcomes Slalom delivered
	• Co-create Org structure and Roles & Responsibilities with the pursuit team and client
	• Design and implement stakeholder alignment approach (tools, processes, etc.)
	• Create approach for measured progress
	• Continue to test and maintain the Big 3 throughout the project
	• Ensure The Big 3 are celebrated (use is rewarded)
